<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cedd</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 620–<a href="/years/664">664</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Saint Cedd</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cedd was a Northumbrian monk trained at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lindisfarne">Lindisfarne</a> who led a mission to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-angles">Middle Angles</a> in 653 and then reconverted the East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxons</a> as their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a>. He founded churches at Bradwell-on-Sea and Tilbury and the monastery of Lastingham in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yorkshire">Yorkshire</a>, and acted as interpreter at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/synod-of-whitby">Synod of Whitby</a> in 664. He died of plague later that year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cedd.jpg" alt="Cedd" width="281" height="401" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saint_cedd.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Saeberht accepted Christianity around 604 and Mellitus became bishop of London, but the kingdom reverted to paganism after his death until <b>Cedd's</b> mission in the 650s.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-essex">Kingdom of Essex</a></li><li><blockquote>Peada brought four priests, including <b>Cedd</b> and Diuma, who preached among the Middle Angles, the first Christian mission in Mercian territory.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-the-middle-angles">Kingdom of the Middle Angles</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in the Kingdom of Northumbria. Died in Lastingham, in what is now <a href="/countries/united-kingdom">the United Kingdom</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=54.3,-0.88&amp;year=648" aria-label="Lastingham on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4531 302 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Cedd"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4981 572h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4981 572h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=54.3,-0.88&amp;year=648">What was here in 648 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
